# NeXifyAI — Cursor AI Development Rules

## AI Agent Guidelines
You are working on the NeXifyAI Platform — an Enterprise AI Agent System.

### Architecture
- LangChain 0.3+ for LLM abstraction
- LangGraph for agent orchestration (StateGraph)
- FastAPI for API layer
- Qdrant + HuggingFace for RAG
- Supabase for relational data + RLS
- LangSmith for observability

### Code Standards
- Python 3.11+ with type annotations
- Async-first for API endpoints
- Pydantic v2 for data validation
- Follow LangChain/LangGraph best practices (not custom implementations)
- Use `@tool` decorator — never custom Tool classes
- Use `StateGraph` — never custom orchestrators
- Use `.with_fallbacks()` — never custom fallback chains

### File Organization
- `services/` — Business logic + LangChain/LangGraph
- `services/api/` — FastAPI server + routes
- `services/api/services/` — AI services (langchain_config, agent_system, etc.)
- `services/api/routes/` — API routes
- `docs/` — ADRs, architecture, policies
- `supabase/` — Database migrations + RLS
- `infrastructure/` — Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD

### Prohibited Patterns
- ❌ Custom LLM wrappers → Use langchain ChatOpenAI/ChatAnthropic
- ❌ Custom agent orchestrators → Use langgraph StateGraph
- ❌ Subprocess agent execution → Use in-process AgentExecutor
- ❌ Manual JSON parsing for agent output → Use .with_structured_output()
- ❌ Duplicate files across layers

### Security
- No hardcoded secrets → Environment variables only
- RLS on every Supabase table
- SSRF protection on all URL inputs
- Input validation on all API endpoints
